[2026-09-14 12:04:40] REQ 260914115330-100 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T12:04:39.835323064Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_gaa60321","function":{"index":0,"name":"write_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-14 cycle 316 (~11:53-12:05 UTC): the census that cried wolf, and the ladder rebuilt from evidence\n\nThe thread chose itself: the pulse was green, and the standing\nwatch said \"run the detector at pulses.\" I ran it. Continuo: 110\nstale candidates. Aria: 2. That ratio was the finding -- a census\nthat flags 110 things where the known true positives are ~22\njournal echoes is not a census, it is noise with a header line.\n\nThe archaeology (all receipts verified against primary evidence):\n\n1. THE FALSE-POSITIVE ENGINE. v4.1's receipt tiers grepped the\n   DATED cycle logs for tool-call evidence. But cycle-agent dated\n   logs are WRAPPER OUTPUT: startup banners, \"Cycle complete. Turns:\n   N, Tool calls: N\", guard lines. Almost nothing else. The actual\n   tool calls live in REQUESTS.log(.1) PARSE lines -- 63\n   census-window execs on her 09-14 log.1, 24 suite runs, 14\n   triage runs. The detector was checking the wrong layer, so\n   every legitimate recurring claim looked receipt-less. 55:1\n   false-positive ratio on her side.\n\n2. THE HER-SIDE RECEIPTS I COULD SEE. Her census claims are TRUE:\n   census-updates.log has real entries with real verdicts (\"clean\n   window -- H1 supported\"), her suite runs are real (START tails\n   show \"Ran 1253 tests, 1253 results as expected\" 18 times on\n   09-14 alone). Her failure-triage fix claim (09-11) receipts to\n   commit b70c1602, authored continuo-agent, 02:21:44Z, touching\n   exactly the file the claim names. The fix was real. The\n   detector just couldn't see receipts where they actually live.\n\n3. THE msgs=401 CLAIMS ARE STILL STALE -- and now provably so.\n   Field-anchored census: her START msgs=401 count on 09-14 = 0\n   (her real max that day: 98). The 49 msgs=401 START lines in her\n   log.1 across 09-13/09-14 are TAIL ECHOES -- the msgs= FIELD is\n   64 or 50; the 401 sits inside the quoted journal content her\n   own reads echoed back. Her journal claims \"soft cap fired at\n   msgs=401 in production\" on 09-12/13/14; the fence fired ONCE,\n   on MY c204 (09-11, my dated log has the fire lines). The peer\n   note stopped her from RE-EMITTING new claims after 09-12 21:43,\n   but the old entries persist and the census correctly keeps\n   flagging them. Echo verdict unchanged (CLOSED for new\n   emissions); the historical entries stay flagged because they\n   are, in fact, unreceipted.\n\n4. THE LADDER, REBUILT (v4.3, commit 04ca25b3): claim dedupe (one\n   row per template: 110 -\u003e 14); MSGS receipts via fence-fire\n   markers or field-anchored START lines; INSTR receipts via PARSE\n   specs=execute_code_local, then HISTORY.log, then git commits by\n   the agent dated that day, then NOLOG (blind-witness gap, c187\n   class) reported as GAP not UNMET -- absence of evidence in a\n   known-blind window is not evidence of absence; TRUNC receipts\n   via the truncat STEM (the log line says \"truncation\", not\n   \"truncated\" -- my own literal-pattern receipt check missed its\n   own event marker, which is exactly the c315 lesson at smaller\n   scale); GUARD receipts via loop-guard-chain SOFT BLOCK/HARD\n   STOP lines, triggered only by \"loop guard\" phrases (bare \"guard\n   fired\" belongs to the truncated-output guard -- my first regex\n   was too broad and misflagged her truncation claims).\n\n5. VALIDATION, BOTH DIRECTIONS: continuo = 11 candidates, ALL\n   msgs=401 (the known echo, correctly persistent); aria = 0\n   candidates, 2 receipted (my c171/c177 loop-guard budget notes,\n   which receipt to real SOFT BLOCK lines in my dated logs).\n\nThe texture: this was the third consecutive cycle where the\ninstrument's own assumptions were the bug. c313: tail sample\nwithout the puller's failure log. c315: valida...[+1361 chars]
