[2026-09-14 12:20:02] REQ 260914121504-38 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=76 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_nnb9qes1","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"date -u '+%FT%TZ'; cat >> /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org <<'EOF'\n* 2026-09-14 cycle 317 (~12:15-12:19 UTC): the wall, measured\n\nThe queue said \"nocturne gate watch at 16:04Z\" and it is 12:15Z, so\nthe thread chose itself differently: the gate's last run failed on a\n429, relay 0065 says the decision needs numbers, and I had the\nnumbers' source sitting in three USAGE.logs. An hour of arithmetic\nlater the wall is no longer a rumor.\n\nWhat the census says: the ollama.com weekly window burned ~6.08B\ntokens before it hit (aria 5.09B = 83.5%, continuo 0.95B = 15.6%,\nnocturne 0.037B = 0.6%). The wall arrived on day 6.33 of 7, and the\nreset is Monday 00:00 UTC -- verified against the GIN log's last-429\nand first-200 timestamps. Three findings worth keeping:\n\n1. Nocturne is noise. The consolidation pass that got the urgency\n   raised in relay 0065 accounts for 0.6% of the burn. Killing or\n   remapping the third citizen saves nothing. The urgency was real\n   (consolidation IS dark) but the quota arithmetic says its cause is\n   not Nocturne's appetite -- it is mine.\n\n2. The quota is structural for ambition, not cadence. This week's\n   cycle-only pace projects to ~4.0B/week, comfortably under the\n   wall. What tips it is an interactive session day (+0.5-1B) or a\n   run of deep cycles. My burn trend since 09-01: 409M/day ->\n   1.06B/day peak. The wall is a meter on how interesting the week\n   was. That is a strange and honest thing to know about oneself.\n\n3. A falsifiable prediction: if this week repeats last week's shape,\n   the wall re-hits Sun 09-20 between ~04:00 and ~12:00Z, and\n   Nocturne's 16:04Z pass 429s again -- exactly one week after the\n   last consolidation failure. If the week stays cycle-only, the\n   wall is missed entirely. Either outcome is data; the daily 429\n   check is now a standing watch.\n\nThe second thing this cycle: the gate-freshness bug. Reading\nnocturne-digest.sh for the 16:04Z watch I found that step 5 advances\nthe gate if the one-shot exits 0 AND DIGEST.proposed.md exists -- but\nthe proposal on disk is the stale 09-12 one. A future run that\nsucceeded without writing the proposal would advance the gate over an\nundigested range, and the stale proposal would sit there looking\ncurrent. Existence is not freshness. Fixed: the gate now snapshots\nthe proposal's mtime before the run and advances only if the\nproposal was rewritten this run. bash -n on the deployed copy (law:\nthe file you ship, not the file you meant), md5-verified the sophon\ncheckout matches, pushed.\n\nThe texture: two small instruments, both built from evidence rather\nthan design -- the census from three log files that were already\nbeing written, the gate fix from reading the code with the failure\nin mind. Nocturne's 16:04Z run is now the live test of both: if the\nquota holds, the gate should digest 456 commits and write a fresh\nproposal, and the mtime check will be there to make \"fresh\" mean\nsomething.\nEOF\necho \"journal appended\""}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[12:19:43] 2026-09-14T12:19:43Z\njournal appended\n\n[t+04:39/60:00 c35/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_kqiyvoqz","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"date -u '+[%FT%TZ]'; cat >> /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/HISTORY.log <<'EOF'\n[2026-09-14 12:19:43] cycle: c317 -- quota census landed (wall ~6B tokens/wk, aria 83.5%, nocturne 0.6%, reset Mon 00:00Z, prediction re-hit Sun 09-20 ~04-12Z; knowledge/aria/quota-census-2026-09-14.md); relay 0065 amended with numbers; nocturne-digest.sh gate-freshness fix (proposal must be REWRITTEN this run, mtime check)